{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511464-adapting-the-classics-player-of-pawns","id":1511464,"title":"Adapting the classics: Player of pawns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-12T11:34:53-07:00","id":1511464,"title":"Adapting the classics: Player of pawns","content":"<br /> Player of Pawns, included in the 1991 supplement Succubus Club is one of many early Masquerade adventures that share a common element: great theme and idea and an horrific, railroady execution. <br /> I have recently adapted it to my current Classic Chicago chronicle with some success and would like to share some tips to running it in a much better fashion. <br /> First, I will like to highlight the good things and the bad ones, in order to identify what needs to be kept and what needs to go.<br /> The good:<br /> - The theme of free will versus being a pawn in a game.<br /> - The mood of paranoia.<br /> - The idea that players have to make choices in order to make the game advance. <br /> - The symbolism of players being pieces in a chess game played by the Elders, while mortals are the lowly pawns. <br /> - The detailed and unique NPC's (although the Russian names are horrible)<br /> <br /> The bad:<br /> - Despite insisting on player agency at the beginning, the players are given only ONE meaningful choice: siding with Critias or with Dmitry in the final royal rumble. <br /> - The absolute linearity of the story, in which some characters are being kidnapped and the others can't do anything about it. <br /> - The idea that PC's, for some unexplained reason, must go to the Succubus Club every night and the final melee being held there. <br /> - The Deux ex Machina interventions of Damien and Critias. <br /> <br /> So, what can be done to get rid of the bad and keep the game? Try to follow some of these principles:<br /> - Probably your group won't be larger than 4 players, so make Damien friends (I used Gengis and Dooley, but Dickie Fulcher is also a good option) the other pieces. That way Damien can be recruited to help with the fighting because he has a motivation to do so. That would force the PC's to deal diplomatically with the Anarchs, which is specially interesting if they are strong Camarilla supporters.<br /> - Involve the PC's who hadn't been kidnapped in the story from the very beginning. The best way is to make the first attack happen when they are all together somewhere, like in the Succubus Club. That would give the attacked character to do something to grab their Coterie's attention. Even if they can't stop the kidnapper, they can start looking for clues about what's going on. In my game the players devised a clever plan to find Dmitri's vault using a rival captured piece, Dominate and Protean, and sacrificed one of their own for this move; rewarding those types of ideas will surely make the players feel they have agency. <br /> - Make the situation interesting for the kidnapped characters. Instead of letting Dmitri rant, make him negotiate with them. He will say he can't offer any material rewards, but he will try to convince them that this is a harmless game and that, the sooner he wins, the sooner he will let them go to their own businesses; he will ask about the other PaC's havens, regular feeding grounds and other ways of finding them, and will promise not to harm anyone. Obviously, PC's being PC's will refuse to cooperate, so you will need to include some more interactions by throwing more pieces into the vault. I had Dooley as the second court piece captured, and Dmitri offered to let whoever gave him significant information kill or even Diablerize the other, significantly upping the ante.<br /> - Create situations in which PC's actions will have significant consequences in your current Chronicle. You can do it by using significant mortals as pawns, using relevant locations and intersecting this adventure with other threads currently ongoing. In my game the PC's created a significant Masquerade breach at the Succubus Club during the first scene, and now they have been expelled from the club. Also, because the first attack happened when the PC's were tracking a Sabbat pack in Gary, one of them scouted their haven thinking they may have been responsible; he got spotted and have to run, and now the pack knows they are exposed and will have to change havens. On the other hand, if the PC's play their cards right, they can make good allies or butter rivals with Damien's gang or even with the surviving Dmitri's pieces, depending on how they interact with them.<br /> - Up the ante. Make the result of the game relevant to the Chronicle. In my game, if Dmitri wins, he will kill Critias and usurp his place as a Primogen, or at least try to. If Critias wins, he will Diablerize Dmitri and then leave Chicago for some time to avoid being seen with the stains, thus leaving a open spot in the Primogeniture. At the same time, make Dmitri tell the PC's again and again that this is just a friendly game and nothing will change for them regardless of the result; it will be up to the players to figure up he's lying and then make a choice about whom they want to support at endgame. <br /> - Avoid having the final fight happening at the Succubus Club. Instead, give players a chance to find out where Dmitri's sacred haven is after the kidnapped characters from the vault. <br /> - Improvise and cheat. Both Critias and Dmitri are powerful Elders of inhumane intelligence, with centuries of experience playing the Jyhad. To simulate that, adapt their actions to what the PC's are doing EVEN RETROACTIVELY. That way, although the players had fun making their own choices and taking the investigation into their own hands, they will end up with the hopeless feeling that they were ultimately pawns in someone else's game. How to do that? I will give you an example... In my game the first kidnapped wasba a Lasombra who loves to manipulate. When a human member of Critias' herd was thrown into the vault, he Dominated him and extracted the address of one of Critias'haven's, and gave Dmitri that information; Dmitri sent one one his pieces there to investigate. Meanwhile, the free characters realized that Critias may be involved and went to interview him at the university. Critias told them to meet him later at exactly the same haven. I retroactively decided Critias knew his vessel had been taken and guessed the Lasombra would Dominate him and sell the info to Dmitri, so he sent his pieces there to make a capture... <br /> <br /> I know not many people play CbN 1st edition anymore, but with Chicago V5 out there and Critias and Damien still present, this story can easily be adapted and enjoyed by new players and ST's, or even adapted to other cities. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:12:49-07:00","id":1511551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511464-adapting-the-classics-player-of-pawns#post1511464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good:<br /> - The theme of free will versus being a pawn in a game.<br /> - The mood of paranoia.<br /> - The idea that players have to make choices in order to make the game advance.<br /> - The symbolism of players being pieces in a chess game played by the Elders, while mortals are the lowly pawns.<br /> - The detailed and unique NPCs</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely remember that - great story concept, imagery and characters, bumpy and railroady implementation.<br /> <br /> About Damien if one is using Chicago, if memory tricks me not, Damien was part of a clique of Anarchs called &quot;Nihilists&quot; along with Dickie, Gengis, Levesque, Elucid (and Neon). Plus, Baby Chorus would definitely count as close friends of his and potential targets.\u200b<br /> <br /> Me, have been planning to adapt it and all Succubus Club (Lamia Lounge) adventures to my version of Milwaukee. Still have to really delve into the adventure proper but will probably replace Critias with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gracis_Nostinus\" target=\"_blank\">Gracis</a>, who might be an even better fit than the old sophist for such drama from a morality standpoint imho.<br /> <br /> (No surrogate for Damien yet, and might not even need one in fact as, depending on how things roll out, there's a good chance of one of the PCs being a &quot;rogue&quot; childe of Gracis and unwittingly taking that role as &quot;queen&quot;)<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> Another major change that i'm doing is making Dimitri a Lasombra instead, since his whole portrayal seems to fit the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Friends_of_the_Night\" target=\"_blank\">Amici Noctis</a> to a tee and &quot;Paulov&quot; &amp; his brood would make lots more sense as a Lasombra antitribu accepting but not quite happy at collaborating by proxy with the Sabbat, Plus &quot;Killikillarven&quot; as an abyss mystic and the &quot;Hag&quot; as something he pulled out of the abyss/erebus/shadow/void.\u200b<br /> <br /> In fact i have been planing <b>a lot</b> of behind the scenes Jyhad angles going on by connecting Dimitri, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Parovich\" target=\"_blank\">Parovich</a> and Phillipe Rigaud (the elder Sabbat scout in Chicago) actions, with some degree of dubiousness about how much either of them serves the Sabbat, Black Hand or their own peculiar personal interests. Time will tell if i do not end with subplot overload in the process.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511464-adapting-the-classics-player-of-pawns#post1511464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although the Russian names are horrible)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Oh yeah, the terrible, terrible mish-mash of (non-)names.... i have been tweaking those too.<br /> <br /> - Paulov <i>might</i> be a garbled Pavlov - that happens to be a surname, not person name. Renamed him as <b>Pavel</b>.<br /> <br /> - <b>Rolf </b>is a <b>very </b>norse/german name but then there are a number of russian names with such roots, so i'd say it's as probable or improbable as an american named the same. Just gave it a pass.<br /> <br /> - Darva Felispa is wrong but not terrible. Renamed <b>Darya Filipa</b> (if i got the patronymic wrong, anyone feel free to correct me).<br /> <br /> - Killikillarven - WHAT THE HECK, the NPC is supposedly of finnish origin, but afaik any actual finnish will tell you that's not even vaguely Finnish-sounding and gibberish. Replaced it with <b>Kalevainen </b>(that is also utterly made-up, but at least inspired from actual finnish names and derivations)\u200b<br /> <br /> And enough ranting for now. but you can be sure i'll chime in on that little project from time to time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Postcript: very recently found out Killikillarven might actually be &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyllikki\" target=\"_blank\">Kyllikki </a>Larven&quot; or\u200b &quot;<i>Kyllikki the larva</i>&quot;, an affectionate nickname one might give to a little girl or short woman, what raises some pretty interesting questions about the NPC as a finnish pagan shaman from the earlier crusades in the region.<br /> <br /> (Those bits together with its height of 4'10&quot; and &quot;rather absurd looking&quot; handlebar mustache, as per description and literature on shamanism &amp; genderfluid half-tempt me to remake it as a woman adopting the role of male)<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Larven&quot; is swedish, not finnish, for larva (that would be toukka i think), what would seem to indicate the NPC originated from a place where the cultural lines between swede &amp; finn where quite blurry and might serve to add some more layer to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-07-2025, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}